/**
\fn pdg::Animated::getMovement()
\brief Read the programmed movement rate.

Returns x/y distance units per second, independently of physical velocity.


\return The current value, returned as a new coordinate object.

\see setMovement(), changeMovementTo(), stopMovement()
*/


/**
\fn pdg::Animated::changeMovementTo(Vector value, number durationSeconds, int easing)
\brief Animate the movement rate to a target.

Uses distance units per second. Duration is the time to reach the new rate, not the lifetime of the motion: the final rate continues until changed or stopped. Dynamic PhysicsBody owners reject this operation. Durations are explicit floating-point seconds. Zero applies immediately; a request after wait() or andThen() must have positive duration.

\param value Movement rate in distance units per second.
\param durationSeconds Finite nonnegative duration in seconds.
\param easing Integer easing constant; elapsed time and duration use seconds.

\return This object, for chaining.

\see setMovement(), changeMovementBy()
*/

/**
\fn pdg::Animated::changeMovementTo(number xPerSecond, number yPerSecond, number durationSeconds, int easing)
\brief Animate the movement rate to a target.

Uses distance units per second. Duration is the time to reach the new rate, not the lifetime of the motion: the final rate continues until changed or stopped. Dynamic PhysicsBody owners reject this operation. Durations are explicit floating-point seconds. Zero applies immediately; a request after wait() or andThen() must have positive duration.

\param xPerSecond Movement rate in distance units per second.
\param yPerSecond Movement rate in distance units per second.
\param durationSeconds Finite nonnegative duration in seconds.
\param easing Integer easing constant; elapsed time and duration use seconds.

\return This object, for chaining.

\see setMovement(), changeMovementBy()
*/




/**
\fn pdg::Animated::setScale(number x, number y)
\brief Set independent transform scale immediately.

Cancels scheduled scale changes. Logical width and height are unchanged. Negative scale reflects an axis; zero collapses it and makes the transform singular. The single-value overload sets both axes. This is an immediate, chainable operation. It throws after wait() or andThen(); only operations with a duration can be part of a timed animation sequence.

\param x Dimensionless scale factor.
\param y Dimensionless scale factor.

\return This object, for chaining.

\see getScale(), changeScaleTo(), changeScaleBy()
*/


/**
\fn pdg::Animated::getScale()
\brief Read independent transform scale.

Returns dimensionless x/y scale factors; the initial factors are (1,1).


\return The current value, returned as a new coordinate object.

\see setScale(), changeScaleTo(), changeScaleBy()
*/


/**
\fn pdg::Animated::changeScaleTo(number x, number y, number durationSeconds, int easing)
\brief Animate independent scale to a target.

Does not change logical size. Negative scale reflects; zero collapses an axis and makes inverse transforms singular. Durations are explicit floating-point seconds. Zero applies immediately; a request after wait() or andThen() must have positive duration.

\param x Dimensionless scale factor.
\param y Dimensionless scale factor.
\param durationSeconds Finite nonnegative duration in seconds.
\param easing Integer easing constant; elapsed time and duration use seconds.

\return This object, for chaining.

\see setScale(), getScale(), changeScaleBy()
*/


/**
\fn pdg::Animated::getStretching()
\brief Read logical width and height change rates.

Returns additive logical units per second for each dimension.


\return The current value, returned as a new coordinate object.

\see setStretching(), changeStretchingTo(), stopStretching()
*/


/**
\fn pdg::Animated::pauseSchedule()
\brief Pause scheduled animations and their delays.

Constant rates, helpers, clips and physics continue. Pausing a rate transition holds its current rate while movement, spin or growth continues at that rate.


\return This object, for chaining.

\see resumeSchedule(), isSchedulePaused(), cancelSchedule()
*/


/**
\fn pdg::Animated::resumeSchedule()
\brief Resume scheduled animations and their delays.

Resumes from the current samples without advancing through the paused time.


\return This object, for chaining.

\see pauseSchedule(), isSchedulePaused()
*/


/**
\fn pdg::Animated::cancelSchedule()
\brief Discard scheduled animations and pending sequencing.

Keeps current values, constant rates and the paused state. Clears pending wait()/andThen() state. AnimatedAttributes also clears appearance and frame transitions.


\return This object, for chaining.

\see hasScheduledAnimations(), pauseSchedule()
*/


/**
\fn pdg::Animated::isSchedulePaused()
\brief Test whether scheduled animation advancement is paused.

This does not report whether constant motion or physics is running.


\return True if scheduled animation is paused.

\see pauseSchedule(), resumeSchedule()
*/


/**
\fn pdg::Animated::hasScheduledAnimations()
\brief Test whether animations are running or queued.

A pending wait() or andThen() alone does not count as a scheduled animation.


\return True if an animation is running or queued.

\see cancelSchedule(), andThen()
*/
